id: pm-hrhfgi
title: "GH-1214: Bound complete item reads and isolate Git newline fixtures on Windows"
description: Nightly Windows Node 24 run 34104192850 exposes unreadable items in the 10000-item aggregate fixture and a CRLF byte mismatch after rebase abort. Preserve complete reads with bounded filesystem concurrency and deterministic repository newline policy.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-07T13:34:48.714Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-07T15:00:55.686Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-07T15:00:55.024Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-07T15:00:55.024Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Complete 10000-item aggregation passes on Windows without shrinking the fixture; bounded descriptor-pressure reads return every readable item; permission failures remain visible; aborted rebase preserves exact fixture bytes and rejects stale Git proof.
goal: project management = context management
value: Reliable complete-corpus SDK queries and portable recovery assurance
why_now: New GitHub report exposes an uncovered boundary in required release or agent workflows.
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Authoritative complete reads use bounded concurrency with genuine read failures preserved. Exact-byte Git fixtures control newline policy, and Bash completion fixtures stream generated scripts through stdin to avoid Windows command-line limits."
expected_result: Complete scans preserve all rows and portable fixtures exercise actual behavior on the supported platform matrix.
actual_result: "Final local correction verified: all 8544 tests in 639 files passed with exact 100/100/100/100 and zero uncovered counts. The complete quality:static chain, linked history suites, strict 12-line/60-token history duplicate scan, docs links and ESLint passed. Fresh npm and Bun installs each passed 15 history workflow steps, SDK execution, sensitive-recovery checks, traversal refusal and oversized-threshold refusal. New exact-head hosted CI, all five Nightly Validation jobs and renewed full review remain required before merge; this is not publication evidence."
